   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Forbidding or saying that you must not",
     "texto": [
      "**-(으)면 안 돼요** means «you can't» or «you must not»: **여기서 음식을 먹으면 안 돼요** = you can't eat here. It is formed with -면 after a vowel or ㄹ, and -으면 after another consonant: **가면**, **살면**, **먹으면**. After ㄹ, the ㄹ is dropped: **만들면 안 돼요**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Compared with -지 마세요",
     "texto": [
      "**-지 마세요** is said to someone as a polite request or order: «please don't do it». **-(으)면 안 돼요** presents a prohibition, rule or consequence: «you can't / you must not». Both forms can appear in public instructions; the context determines which one fits better."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
